      "textEn": "272\n\nMeaning: It is known from the Brahma-Samhita that Shri Bhagavan is the cause of all causes (Sarva-karana-\nkaranam). Rishabhdev was the first incarnation of Lord Vishnu, the father of Krishna. Their son Bharat\nTo the king, who was now playing the role of Brahmin Jad Bharat, his body was obtained by the cause of those very causes; therefore, he is called Karan-Vigrahaya. Like the fire of a burning desire, truthful,\nLike the snow that melts in the heat of the sun. Those who have seen the self-illuminating,\nI am the nectar-like medicine for those who are in the state of Brahman. 2. Meaning of the word\n\nFever—fever, or of heat; Aamay—of disease; Aartasya—of the afflicted man; Yatha—as; Agadam—medicine; Sat—correct; Nidagh-Daghastya—on being afflicted with fever; Yatha—as; Him-Ambhah—very cold water; Ku-Deha—in this body, which is like excrement and urine; Man—like pride; Ah-Serpent; Vidhast—bitten, struck; Drishteah—of the seer; Brahman—He\nThe best among Brahmins; Vachah—word, speech; Te—yours; Amrutam—nectar; Vidhast—bitten; Kasht—difficult; Vachah—word; Ta-Ta—your; Amrutam—nectar; Vidhast—bitten; Kasht—difficult; Vachah—word; Ta-Ta—your; Amrutam—nectar;\nOh, best of Brahmins, my body is full of filth, and my sight is bitten by a serpent in the form of pride. Because of my\nphysical intelligence, I am sick. For a person suffering from this type of fever, your\nnectar-like teachings are just like cool water for a person scorched by the sun (loo). Meaning: The body of a corpse is filled with impure things—bones, blood, urine, feces, etc. So,\neven the intelligent men of this world think that they are made up of the combination of blood, bone, blood, urine, and feces. If that is the case, then why not the same materials to produce other intelligent beings? The entire world is overwhelmed by bodily consciousness, and even for good people, hellish conditions are being created for living. The teachings that Jad Bharat gave to King Rahugan are ex